From: SF2000 Linux <sf2000@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] qpsx: gate the MIPS32r2 GPU helpers explicitly

QPSX treats every MIPS target as able to call gpu_inner_mips32.S, but that
file declares MIPS32r2 and uses EXT. HC15xx implements MIPS32r1. Let the Linux
port select the existing C fallbacks while retaining the MIPS dynarec and the
MIPS32r1 CDDA mixer.

diff --git a/src/gpu/gpu_unai/gpu_inner_mips32.h b/src/gpu/gpu_unai/gpu_inner_mips32.h
index 151e1b4..29e7412 100644
--- a/src/gpu/gpu_unai/gpu_inner_mips32.h
+++ b/src/gpu/gpu_unai/gpu_inner_mips32.h
@@ -19,7 +19,8 @@
  * All functions are optional - controlled via menu toggles.
  * When disabled, falls back to C implementations.
  */
 
-#if defined(SF2000) || defined(__mips__)
+#if (defined(SF2000) || defined(__mips__)) && \
+    !defined(QPSX_DISABLE_MIPS32R2_GPU_ASM)
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 extern "C" {
